1
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:11,120
Just try keeping your distance, will you?

2
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:24,300
Anyone without money, come to my place!

3
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:28,980
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at the blue sky

5
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:36,320
white clouds

6
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:42,840
Somehow or other, it'll all work out.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to my place!

8
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:04,560
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:11,960
The burning crimson clouds too

10
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow or other, it'll all work out.

11
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Right, right.

12
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,440
Once you get it, keep quiet and follow me.

13
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:52,340
In any case, there are growing concerns about
juvenile crime involving ever-younger offenders.

14
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:54,560
And that's all for tonight.

15
00:01:56,280 --> 00:02:00,200
Juvenile crime is getting younger

16
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,340
As parents of kids ourselves,
it's not someone else's problem, is it?

17
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:06,240
Honey, you're in the way.
Can you move? I'm laying out the futons.

18
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,200
Okay, okay.

19
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:12,500
Honestly, we finally moved into a house,
so why are you sitting in the corner?

20
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:16,880
Well, it's just too spacious. I can't
relax unless there's a wall behind me.

21
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:18,300
You're so stingy with yourself.

22
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,860
By the way, what are the kids up to?

23
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:24,480
They were playing games until just now,
but they've probably gone to bed by now.

24
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:25,620
I see.

25
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:30,500
They're sleeping well

26
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:33,080
Well, as for our child,
there's no need to worry.

27
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,160
They've been playing games at home.

28
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:44,280
It's summer vacation,
so I wish they'd take us somewhere to play.

29
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:49,280
I heard Shinji went to
Hawaii with all his dads.

30
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:51,440
I want to go somewhere too.

31
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:57,340
I heard Yoshiko went to the
mountains in the countryside.

32
00:02:57,740 --> 00:03:00,020
I want to catch cicadas or stag beetles too.

33
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:06,300
I heard Harrow went to the sea to
go fishing and set off fireworks.

34
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:10,140
I love the sea too,
so I'd like to go fishing there.

35
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:21,540
What's with that stern face?

36
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:24,120
Unno Kizu,
who earned her boating license at 40,

37
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:27,540
enjoys cruising with her family on weekends.

38
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:31,820
Connecting with nature, which you can't
experience in the city, is the best.

39
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:35,980
Everything from the beauty of the stars seen at sea
is so moving.

40
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:41,240
With this, I don't worry that the children will
fall into juvenile delinquency.

41
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:45,300
I really think it was good
that we bought the cruiser.

42
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:47,400
Staying overnight on the boat is fun!

43
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,920
Daddy's amazing!

44
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:51,860
The other day,
I caught a big fish like this!

45
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:54,760
This one!

46
00:03:57,260 --> 00:03:59,000
Papa's the young boss.

47
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:03,420
What? You bought a boat?

48
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,880
There's no need to be so surprised,
is there?

49
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:08,860
What's wrong, Terai?

50
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,920
I've finally given up on life!

51
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:13,700
D-don't do anything rash!

52
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,920
I'm not doing anything rash.

53
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:20,400
Mr. Terai,
you have a life that's right for you.

54
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:21,860
That's right, Mr. Terai.

55
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:25,800
That's just it. I've been wondering
what my life has amounted to so far.

56
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:31,500
I was so busy with work that I
had no time to spend with my kids,

57
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:35,640
and I never had anything
you could even call a hobby.

58
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:44,240
I was thinking we should buy a boat and
spend time in nature for the kids' upbringing.

59
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,300
So you suddenly went for a cruiser

60
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:50,360
You, who's played it safe your
whole life with sacrifice bunts,

61
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:53,620
down by one run, bases loaded with
two outs in the bottom of the ninth,

62
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:56,360
you're pulling off a
squeeze play to steal home!

63
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,780
Shut up.

64
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:00,780
Terai's thinking about it in his own way.

65
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,900
Probably Terai.

66
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:03,360
Haah.

67
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:07,640
Speaking of which,
the first time I rode my father's cruiser,

68
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,900
We have such happy memories, don't we?

69
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:14,280
Yes, Daddy's back looked bigger
and more rugged than usual.

70
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:17,400
Right? Just like Yuzo Kayama
in the Young Master films.

71
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:21,040
As a father and as a man,
I want to try riding a cruiser.

72
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,492
What's this "Young Master" nonsense?

73
00:05:22,542 --> 00:05:26,300
You're the man in all of Japan
who suits a cruiser the least.

74
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:31,860
That's not true. Even if you can't be Yuzo Kayama,
you could manage to be Kunie Tanaka's Aodaisho.

75
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:35,240
Your references are too old.
We can't keep up.

76
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,320
Seriously.

77
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:39,900
Do you even know how much a cruiser costs?

78
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:42,440
It's so expensive,
your eyes would pop out of your head.

79
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:49,280
We've got a special offer, this one!
Perfect for the salaryman dad!

80
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:56,140
A cruiser for every family!
Ryo-san's cruiser, it's a cruiser!

81
00:05:56,140 --> 00:06:00,520
I know, but can a salaryman
really afford this on his salary?

82
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:05,680
Yes, welcome!
All of our cruisers are top-of-the-line.

83
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:09,040
We have only the finest selection. You...

84
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:13,580
A fake real estate agent
and a fake travel agency, too.

85
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:17,180
Well, well, what are you talking about?

86
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:21,180
Looking to buy a cruiser?

87
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:24,160
But it still looks expensive.

88
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:26,060
There's no need to worry.

89
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:29,360
This cruiser, which we proudly offer,

90
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:31,380
normally priced at 80 million yen,

91
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:33,680
is only 40 million yen!

92
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:36,740
80 million yen cut in half to 40 million,
a 50% discount!

93
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:38,040
Can you afford it?

94
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,820
For customers like you,
we also have even cheaper models.

95
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,480
Right this way.

96
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:50,200
Normally 80 million yen,
now a bargain 10 million yen!

97
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:52,320
That's 10 million yen off, Ryo-san.

98
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:58,120
And right now, you also get a hanging exercise
bar and a kombucha mushroom tea thrown in!

99
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,800
Even better value!

100
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:03,820
Alright, let's sign the contract right away.
It's 10 million yen.

101
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,540
10 million yen

102
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:08,580
If it's a loan, maybe I can manage.

103
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:19,680
Wait, you should check the loan terms more carefully.
No way, sir. Now is the time. If you let this slip, the cruiser will belong to someone else.

104
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:31,660
Right, the early bird gets the worm! Now hurry up and sign here.
Hold on, hold on... What if it's a 1/1 scale model kit?

105
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:32,720
That's it!

106
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,480
Isn't it just the same thing?

107
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:37,180
A model kit.

108
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:41,760
Just as I thought.

109
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:44,340
Isn't that a Maguchi underwater motor?

110
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:46,000
Are you planning to run it on batteries?

111
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:49,480
And the burrs alone are
thirty centimeters long.

112
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:51,240
A shoddy model kit like this one

113
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,860
You're really going to
sell it for 10 million yen?

114
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:54,300
No way, that's absurd.

115
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,800
It was just a joke, that's all.

116
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:57,560
The real one is over here.

117
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,520
This is the true real deal.

118
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:04,280
Wow, it's huge and magnificent!

119
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:07,740
No, no, we can't be sure yet.
Those could be sheet metal burrs.

120
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:13,600
Come on, sign here quickly.
If you dawdle, it'll sell out!

121
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:20,100
Look closely! There's a seam here
where they joined it to another boat.

122
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:23,910
I thought something was off.
They did a good job disguising the outside,

123
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:26,740
but the color subtly
changes on the bottom here.

124
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:29,860
No, that's two-tone coloring,
which is all the rage now.

125
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:34,860
Two wires, see?
They must have stuck two pieces together.

126
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:37,900
Alright, I'll make it cheaper.
5 million yen.

127
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:38,520
Too expensive!

128
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:39,720
3 million.

129
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:40,920
Still too much.

130
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,600
2 million yen.

131
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:45,800
1 million yen.
I won't pay a single penny more.

132
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,420
1 million yen.

133
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,060
Deal, 1 million yen.

134
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:50,020
Yes.

135
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:52,720
Good, change this to 1 million yen.

136
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:53,820
Yes.

137
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,920
Good, sign it, Terai.

138
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,380
Are you sure about this?

139
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:02,100
Yes.

140
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,040
Is this okay?

141
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:07,240
Yes, that's fine.

142
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:10,100
Yes! Now the cruiser is mine!

143
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,900
It's all thanks to me, you know.

144
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:16,580
When it's first unveiled,
you'd better invite me on a free cruise.

145
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:18,500
Thanks, Ryo-san.

146
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:21,340
I never thought I'd get it
for just one million yen.

147
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:34,820
We got the boat license and the marina berth too,
so that's great.

148
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:40,060
I can really picture
Terai's kids being so happy.

149
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:44,540
When it comes to cruising,
I have nothing but happy memories.

150
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:54,060
Me too.

151
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:03,400
You lot, try imagining something
a little more down-to-earth.

152
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,380
At least,

153
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:08,580
something like this, you know.

154
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:12,500
Right, Terai is the star of the show.

155
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:23,100
Alright, let's set sail!

156
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,720
Hang on a second.

157
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:27,100
The name isn't good.

158
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:31,000
A name like Blue Max
doesn't suit you at all.

159
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,300
Yeah, this'll do.

160
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:38,020
A sacrifice bunt in life?

161
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:41,240
That's the perfect name for you.

162
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,280
N-no way.

163
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:46,700
Former Splashdown

164
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:48,460
It's floating.

165
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:49,800
Of course it is.

166
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:51,920
Yoisho, Captain!

167
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:53,000
No way, I don't want that.

168
00:10:54,060 --> 00:10:57,360
Out at sea,
the captain is the most important person.

169
00:10:57,360 --> 00:11:00,640
Everyone has to listen
to what the captain says.

170
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,600
Yes, sir.

171
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:05,500
All responsibility rests with the captain.

172
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:07,580
All the responsibility is on me?

173
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,500
Hang in there, dear.

174
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,060
Alright!

175
00:11:11,060 --> 00:11:14,060
Terai, show me the cabin before we set off.

176
00:11:14,060 --> 00:11:16,480
Yeah, look, it's really spacious!

177
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:18,460
Right this way.

178
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:21,540
W-what?

179
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:25,160
It's spacious, right?
It's twice the size of our old house.

180
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:27,320
Damn, we got taken.

181
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:30,136
At night we sleep in
sleeping bags in the tent,

182
00:11:30,186 --> 00:11:32,180
and cook over a shichirin at night too!

183
00:11:32,180 --> 00:11:34,340
No, really, cruisers are great, aren't they?

184
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:35,980
It's just like camping!

185
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:38,640
So that's why it was priced that way.

186
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:42,560
But Terai seems to think
this is the real thing.

187
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:43,960
Let's keep quiet about it.

188
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:44,460
Yeah.

189
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,220
So small!

190
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:50,740
Lots of boats here.

191
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:53,680
This is the only marina
that's cheap and close by.

192
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:56,040
How's it going? Looks like
you're about to hit the left side!

193
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:00,020
Daddy, you'll hit this side too!

194
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:02,340
Now it's this side!

195
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:04,020
It's no different from
parking a car in a garage.

196
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:06,740
If you hit someone else's boat,
it'll be a huge problem.

197
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:08,100
Right, right, watch out!

198
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,980
Terai, you're pretty good at this!

199
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:19,460
For a first timer,
you've got good instincts.

200
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:20,400
R-really?

201
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:22,140
Alright!

202
00:12:29,060 --> 00:12:32,660
T-Terai! Going too fast is dangerous!

203
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:34,880
There are obstacles at sea too!

204
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:37,880
Stop driving recklessly, you selfish fool!

205
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,960
This thrilling rush!

206
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:43,400
I'm the captain! I'm a man of the sea!

207
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,160
We'll christen it with beer!

208
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,120
Me too.

209
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,100
Stay calm and don't rush.

210
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:10,220
Yay!

211
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:13,280
Wow!

212
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:14,740
Alright!

213
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:17,720
Then I'll use this to make
something incredibly delicious

214
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,060
and make you some sushi.

215
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:23,460
Make the kisu over here into tempura.

216
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:25,260
Let's make the flavor tataki.

217
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,980
Leave it to me, Pyo-chan.

218
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:33,720
Wow, this is delicious!

219
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,400
The freshness really makes a difference,
doesn't it?

220
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:39,000
Right? This is a taste you can
only get by going out to sea.

221
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,540
Even though you didn't
catch a single fish yourself.

222
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:44,660
But it's thanks to my cruiser, isn't it?

223
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:45,820
Well, I suppose that's true.

224
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:52,800
Still, there sure are a lot
of cruisers and yachts around.

225
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:56,320
And they're all high-end ones, too.

226
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:00,820
Hello.

227
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:02,060
Hi there.

228
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:03,440
Wow, that looks delicious.

229
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:06,720
Sushi made from fish just caught,
how lavish!

230
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:07,280
No.

231
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:10,600
Right, we can't just
leave this sitting here.

232
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:16,520
What, you're going to make
deliveries using this cruiser?

233
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:18,480
What's going on, Ryo-chan?

234
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:22,480
On this Jinsei Okuri Bunto-gō,
we go around to each cruiser

235
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:24,640
and make freshly caught fish into sushi

236
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:26,800
or fillet it into sashimi.

237
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:30,760
We also deliver seafood
and vegetables on request.

238
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:33,420
In other words,
we're a handyman service for the sea.

239
00:14:33,420 --> 00:14:35,340
But why are you doing something like that?

240
00:14:35,460 --> 00:14:36,140
Well, that's

241
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:38,660
Well, it's to pay off our loans along with

242
00:14:38,660 --> 00:14:43,240
helping Terai, who's suffering
in the loan hell of this cruiser.

243
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:44,200
Right, Terai?

244
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:45,320
Fish-san

245
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,760
Sorry for the constant disturbance.

246
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:55,820
To all of you enjoying fishing and
diving on your cruisers and yachts,

247
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:59,803
we'll turn your freshly caught
fish into fresh sashimi and sushi,

248
00:14:59,853 --> 00:15:01,660
cooked right here on the spot.

249
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:04,200
Please feel free to give us a call.

250
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:07,351
We also offer jet skis, scuba gear,

251
00:15:07,401 --> 00:15:09,540
goldfish food, portable burners, and more.

252
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,300
So freshly caught fish becomes fresh sashimi

253
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,020
Sounds good.

254
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,560
Hey, we'll take one over here.

255
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:14,340
Yes, thank you for your business.

256
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,580
We'll take one over here too.

257
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:16,160
Thanks.

258
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:17,540
Hey, Terai.

259
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:20,140
Dock between those two cruisers.

260
00:15:20,780 --> 00:15:21,140
Right.

261
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:24,080
Idiot, not that way!

262
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:44,420
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

263
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:47,540
Hey, are we making sashimi? Or sushi?

264
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:51,460
Well, I think sashimi is best after all.

265
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:52,740
Make it this one.

266
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:53,480
Coming right up.

267
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,420
Could you make this one into sushi?

268
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:56,800
Here you go, thanks for the business.

269
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:59,600
Get the rice ready right away.

270
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:02,760
Don't just stand there,
have your wife and kids help too.

271
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:07,100
Honestly, we're doing this
for the daily loan payments!

272
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:08,440
Wh-, got it.

273
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,660
Give me the agari.

274
00:16:09,660 --> 00:16:10,960
Agari-cho.

275
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:11,520
Akadashi.

276
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:12,460
Make it akadashi.

277
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:13,100
Yes, and then...

278
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:15,440
Hokkaido gōsan is delicious!

279
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:19,060
Nakagawa, we're broke!
Have it flown in from Hokkaido!

280
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:21,520
Reiko, where are my ten cakes?

281
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,860
Ma'am, smile more cheerfully.

282
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:25,840
Terai, you're in the way, you're in the way!

283
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,780
51, 52, and...

284
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:38,840
Terai, time to split the earnings.

285
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:41,640
So we actually made a decent profit.

286
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,860
Yeah. So, Terai, you get 5% of the profit.

287
00:16:44,860 --> 00:16:45,440
Thank you.

288
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:49,600
Come on, senior, 5% is just too cruel.

289
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:53,460
That's right. Why does Ryo-chan take 95%?

290
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:55,100
I'm the one who came up with the idea.

291
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:57,640
I'm also the one who sliced
the sashimi and made the sushi.

292
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,960
And this includes my management fee.

293
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:01,560
That's just terrible.

294
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:03,840
The boat belongs to Terai, after all.

295
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,740
At the very least,
it should be a fifty-fifty split.

296
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:10,220
Ryo-san, it would really help if at
least the repair costs were covered.

297
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:16,000
Right, so no repair money... thanks a lot.

298
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:28,600
You poor guy... Why are you wearing
a coat in this midsummer heat?

299
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:33,340
It's stifling. An Armani jacket and coat.

300
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:38,280
The tie's Fratex, the shoes are Hera-something,
all told, ten million yen.

301
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:40,440
Even in midsummer, good things are good.

302
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:44,020
Anyway, I see you're still squabbling over small change,
as always.

303
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:44,640
Me.

304
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,040
What the hell is this?

305
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:57,340
Not another kids' bank note, though.

306
00:17:57,340 --> 00:17:59,700
My body just reacted on its own.

307
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:02,800
Gimme, gimme.

308
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,920
By the way, I have a question.

309
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:09,340
What's that duck-shaped pedal
boat floating on the lake?

310
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:11,440
How awful, my cruiser...

311
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:12,420
Cruiser.

312
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:18,820
A cruiser is the kind of boat
a super-rich guy like me rides.

313
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:22,100
Sure, that one over
there is many times bigger.

314
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,520
And it looks cool.

315
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:26,260
It's not about looks, for men or cruisers.

316
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:30,380
Do you really think you can
beat my lifetime-payment loan?

317
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:33,480
You're Daddy.

318
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:38,440
Let's race! Whoever gets under
that lighthouse first wins.

319
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:49,800
Yeah, sure! Eigo-san, you'll be mine soon!
Why do you bring me into this?

320
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:56,300
Ugh...

321
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:58,940
Start!

322
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:04,640
It's not starting!

323
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:08,520
Okay.

324
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:16,980
Looks like it stalled.

325
00:19:16,980 --> 00:19:19,800
Driving a boat and he's this terrible at it?

326
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:23,700
Yeah, I warned him to be careful,
since it's for super-rich owners!

327
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:24,680
Come on, start up!

328
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:28,060
Good, good boy.

329
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:30,600
Reiko-san!

330
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:33,080
Yahoo!

331
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:41,940
Finally, we're underway!

332
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:46,600
Damn it, we won't give up!

333
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,760
They're catching up!

334
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:58,560
Here they come! Terai, go faster!

335
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:04,720
How about that?

336
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:10,380
Damn it, Terai!
We're falling further behind!

337
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:11,900
Speed it up!

338
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:12,820
Got it.

339
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:17,440
Dear!

340
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:19,420
What's wrong, Terai?

341
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:21,200
I'm seasick.

342
00:20:28,180 --> 00:20:29,620
Are you all right, Mr. Terai?

343
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:32,940
Hang in there, dear!

344
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:35,000
Right, you two, look after Terai!

345
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,280
Ryo-san, can you even drive this?

346
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:41,540
Please, this is just like driving a car.

347
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:43,060
Just a little here, a little there.

348
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:43,800
Whoops!

349
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:45,720
Here we go!

350
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:49,660
Nice!

351
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:04,920
Alright, I can see it now!

352
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:09,900
They've caught up already?

353
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:12,520
Alright, full speed ahead!

354
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:14,620
Get back here, you bastard!

355
00:21:18,260 --> 00:21:19,260
That's it for you.

356
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:20,560
Yaaah!

357
00:21:23,460 --> 00:21:25,700
Yahhahahaha! How about that!

358
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:28,340
Damn it, we can't beat them on speed!

359
00:21:33,420 --> 00:21:36,840
Alright,
let's settle this with tight turns! Yaaah!

360
00:21:37,820 --> 00:21:38,540
Aaaaah!

361
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:49,460
Eeeeeeee

362
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:52,580
Aaaaaaaa

363
00:21:52,580 --> 00:21:54,140
Aaaaaaaa

364
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:55,840
Aaaaaaaa

365
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:57,620
Aaaaaaaa

366
00:21:57,620 --> 00:21:57,780
Aaaaaaaa

367
00:21:58,740 --> 00:22:27,020


368
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:31,980
Eeh

369
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:34,660
Hey, are you okay?!

370
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:36,760
Yeah, I'm fine!

371
00:22:38,580 --> 00:22:39,100
What?

372
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,220
Thank goodness.

373
00:23:25,380 --> 00:23:29,520
With this compensation,
we'll be super-poor again, I guess.

374
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:42,820
My life's sacrifice bunt...

375
00:23:42,820 --> 00:23:46,740
It split in two and sank into the sea.

376
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:51,320
Pull yourself together!

377
00:23:52,700 --> 00:23:54,780
Today, Daddy's cruiser...

378
00:23:54,780 --> 00:23:58,020
split clean in two and sank into the sea.

379
00:23:58,020 --> 00:24:00,080
Daddy fainted.

380
00:24:31,620 --> 00:24:34,180
A strange feeling

381
00:24:34,940 --> 00:24:35,620
So

382
00:24:36,380 --> 00:24:39,620
on the arcade guide tiles

383
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:45,440
I tried walking only on the black parts

384
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:51,580
Everyone was a child once,

385
00:24:51,580 --> 00:24:53,540
but everyone forgets

386
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:57,640
Not for pompous-faced politicians,

387
00:24:57,640 --> 00:25:00,960
or blue-eyeshadowed aunties either

388
00:25:01,620 --> 00:25:06,600
Turn that corner, go on,

389
00:25:07,580 --> 00:25:11,800
you'll meet everyone, everyone

390
00:25:12,380 --> 00:25:19,760
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari

391
00:25:21,020 --> 00:25:25,060
Come on, everyone, to our town

392
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:26,560
Thank you

393
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:40,900
Thank you!

